{
  "id": "binary_prefix_divisible_by_5",
  "title": "Binary Prefix Divisible By 5",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Algorithms",
  "tags": [
    "Array",
    "Bit Manipulation"
  ],
  "description": "<p>You are given a binary array <code>nums</code> (<strong>0-indexed</strong>).</p> <p>We define <code>x<sub>i</sub></code> as the number whose binary representation is the subarray <code>nums[0..i]</code> (from most-significant-bit to least-significant-bit).</p> <ul> <li>For example, if <code>nums = [1,0,1]</code>, then <code>x<sub>0</sub> = 1</code>, <code>x<sub>1</sub> = 2</code>, and <code>x<sub>2</sub> = 5</code>.</li> </ul> <p>Return <em>an array of booleans </em><code>answer</code><em> where </em><code>answer[i]</code><em> is </em><code>true</code><em> if </em><code>x<sub>i</sub></code><em> is divisible by </em><code>5</code>.</p> <p> </p> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums = [0,1,1]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [true,false,false]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The input numbers in binary are 0, 01, 011; which are 0, 1, and 3 in base-10.\nOnly the first number is divisible by 5, so answer[0] is true.\n</pre> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums = [1,1,1]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [false,false,false]\n</pre> <p> </p> <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>1 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 10<sup>5</sup></code></li> <li><code>nums[i]</code> is either <code>0</code> or <code>1</code>.</li> </ul>",
  "hints": [
    "If X is the first i digits of the array as a binary number, then 2X + A[i] is the first i+1 digits."
  ],
  "method": {
    "name": "prefixesDivBy5",
    "returnType": "auto",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "nums",
        "type": "array"
      }
    ]
  },
